# Copied to augmentor/.env by whoever runs Augmentor. Two consumers: the bridge
# merges this into the runtime's process environment (existing env wins), and the
# runtime's DSH credentials provider uses it as its last-resort fallback layer.
#
# Which models the sidecar offers is NOT configured here — the runtime loads
# $DSH_HOME/settings.yaml (default ~/.dsh/settings.yaml), the SAME document the
# DSH app loads, so the extension's model picker always mirrors the DSH app:
# the llm-pi-ai provider routes there (local models) plus the built-in DeepSeek
# route. Each route's key is resolved by name through the DSH credentials seam:
#   inherited process environment  >  ~/.dsh/.credentials.yaml  >  this .env
#
# Configure provider routes in DSH's Models page. Prefer its credential store or
# environment variables supplied privately by the launching shell.
#
# Example only: use the environment-variable name referenced by your route.
# LOCAL_MODEL_API_KEY=
#
# DEEPSEEK_API_KEY is resolved from DSH's credential store by default. Set it
# privately only if the configured route needs an environment fallback:
# DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=
